    "title": {
     "en": "Sharing with leftovers"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "If 13 sweets are shared among 4 children, each gets 3 and 1 is left over."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "divide",
     "remainder",
     "quotient",
     "leftover"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Division is sharing into equal groups.\nWhen the sharing is not exact, something is left over. The leftover is called the remainder.\n13 ÷ 4 = 3 remainder 1, because 4 × 3 = 12 and 13 - 12 = 1.\nThe remainder is always smaller than the divisor.\nCheck: quotient × divisor + remainder = number."
    }
   },
